WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:03.660
Tidepath Family Alliance: a made-up Miami nonprofit with 7 staff roles and 1 operator, Alex.

2
00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:04.710
Roomcord: the private workspace where staff work. Each room has one AI agent for one job.

3
00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:07.933
Tidepath works in 9 rooms, one job and one AI agent each.

4
00:00:07.983 --> 00:00:10.067
Kids and families: Programs, Volunteers, Workshops, Counseling.

5
00:00:10.117 --> 00:00:12.067
Money: Fundraising, and Grants and finance.

6
00:00:12.117 --> 00:00:14.393
Director desk routes work. People CRM holds every record.

7
00:00:14.433 --> 00:00:15.693
P5. Volunteer hours get lost, and urgent needs wait for days.

8
00:00:15.733 --> 00:00:16.743
The Tidepath portal: a public website with no login. Volunteers, parents and schools use it on a phone.

9
00:00:16.783 --> 00:00:19.733
Maria opens the check-in form in Spanish.

10
00:00:19.783 --> 00:00:23.700
She logs 1 hour with Kevin and flags an urgent need: a laptop.

11
00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:26.410
She taps Send. No login, no app to install.

12
00:00:26.450 --> 00:00:28.533
Maria's check-in arrives in the Volunteers room.

13
00:00:28.583 --> 00:00:31.767
The agent logs the hour once and flags the laptop as urgent.

14
00:00:31.817 --> 00:00:34.233
Alex asks the Director agent to send it to Programs.

15
00:00:34.283 --> 00:00:37.033
The Director agent posts the need in Programs and mentoring.

16
00:00:37.083 --> 00:00:39.110
Programs and mentoring now shows a new message.

17
00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:40.300
Alex opens Programs and mentoring.

18
00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:43.527
The urgent need is here the same day, with a mention for Alex.

19
00:00:43.567 --> 00:00:44.777
P1. Kids at risk get missed until it is too late.

20
00:00:44.817 --> 00:00:47.000
Alex asks the Programs agent: who needs a call this week?

21
00:00:47.050 --> 00:00:49.000
The agent checks attendance and mentor meetings in the CRM.

22
00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:52.033
Kevin and Jaylen missed sessions. They need a call this week.

23
00:00:52.083 --> 00:00:54.267
Alex asks for a follow-up to Kevin's mother, in Spanish.

24
00:00:54.317 --> 00:00:56.200
The agent writes the draft.

25
00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:59.193
It says DRAFT, not sent. A person approves before anything goes out.

26
00:00:59.233 --> 00:01:00.243
The People CRM app runs inside the Roomcord room 'People CRM'. Staff review records and approve.

27
00:01:00.283 --> 00:01:01.833
Alex opens the People CRM tab.

28
00:01:01.883 --> 00:01:04.900
67 people in one list: kids, parents, mentors, volunteers, donors.

29
00:01:04.950 --> 00:01:07.767
Duplicates: records that may be the same person.

30
00:01:07.817 --> 00:01:10.367
Rosa Delgado is in twice: same phone, same address.

31
00:01:10.417 --> 00:01:12.700
Alex clicks Approve merge.

32
00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:15.700
The record keeps who approved, the time and the history.

33
00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:18.667
This week: at-risk kids, each with a draft follow-up.

34
00:01:18.717 --> 00:01:21.367
Alex approves Kevin's follow-up.

35
00:01:21.417 --> 00:01:24.267
Approved by Alex, with the time. The owner calls the parent.

36
00:01:24.317 --> 00:01:26.633
Q3 report: the numbers that funders ask for.

37
00:01:26.683 --> 00:01:29.860
Every total is counted again from the raw rows, and every check matches.

38
00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:31.110
P2. Regular donors stop giving, and nobody notices.

39
00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:33.233
Alex asks which regular donors are late.

40
00:01:33.283 --> 00:01:35.167
The agent checks each donor's giving schedule.

41
00:01:35.217 --> 00:01:38.827
Two donors are late: a monthly gift by 35 days, a 90-day gift by 31.

42
00:01:38.867 --> 00:01:40.077
P3. Schools wait days for answers about workshops.

43
00:01:40.117 --> 00:01:44.133
A school counselor requests a safety workshop, in Spanish.

44
00:01:44.183 --> 00:01:46.543
She sends it. She does not need an account.

45
00:01:46.583 --> 00:01:48.900
The request arrives in the Workshop requests room.

46
00:01:48.950 --> 00:01:51.843
The agent asks every missing question in one reply and opens W002.

47
00:01:51.883 --> 00:01:56.443
Later, the school approves slides v2 on the portal.

48
00:01:56.483 --> 00:01:58.433
The approval arrives in the room.

49
00:01:58.483 --> 00:02:00.993
The tracker records school approved v2, and who approved it.

50
00:02:01.033 --> 00:02:02.243
P4. Counseling notes are private, but funders need numbers.

51
00:02:02.283 --> 00:02:05.467
Alex asks what exactly goes to the funder from a sample note.

52
00:02:05.517 --> 00:02:08.933
Will be sent: only service facts, like date, minutes, ZIP and age band.

53
00:02:08.983 --> 00:02:11.060
Stays inside: names, the narrative and risk flags.

54
00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:12.310
P6. Grant spending is hard to track against the funder rules.

55
00:02:12.350 --> 00:02:15.333
Alex asks what is left per category in the county grant.

56
00:02:15.383 --> 00:02:17.267
The agent reads the grant budget and the spending.

57
00:02:17.317 --> 00:02:19.827
Emergency aid has $800 left. No category is over 90%.

58
00:02:19.867 --> 00:02:20.877
How it is built: the source code is open on GitHub.

59
00:02:20.917 --> 00:02:25.267
One repository holds every agent, skill, the portal and the CRM app.

60
00:02:25.317 --> 00:02:29.660
Each agent is a flavor: role + rules + skills.

61
00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:32.550
Every detail entered once. Urgent needs reach staff the same day. Reports in minutes. A human approves everything.
